# The sandbox RDS alarm catalogue, as environment variables.
#
# The 20 `rds-alerts` definitions and their 53 severity rules, transcribed from the CloudWatch
# alarm rules the infrastructure repository owns:
#
#   hyperswitch-infra @ f95b37ad9
#   terraform/aws/live/sandbox/ap-south-1/cloudwatch-alarms/terragrunt.hcl
#
# Dimension values are resolved: all three RDS dimension sets are literals declared in that
# region's `database/terragrunt.hcl` (`hyperswitchdb-cluster`, `hyperswitchdb-primary`,
# `failover-replica-1`), so nothing here was read out of Terraform state.
#
# Values omitted upstream are materialised here, because the Terraform module fills them in before
# the AWS alarms are created and this service refuses a rule that does not say what it evaluates:
# period 60, statistic Average, comparison operator GreaterThanThreshold, evaluation periods 5,
# missing-data policy notBreaching. The two `rds-alerts` anomaly definitions are absent — they
# compare against a band rather than a threshold, and this service does not evaluate them.
#
# TEMPORARY, and not a second source of truth: hyperswitch-cloud#23444 renders these from
# Terraform into the deployment's configuration, at which point this file is deleted. Refresh it by
# re-transcribing from the catalogue rather than by editing a threshold here.
#
# Ids are lowercase and `_`-separated because an environment variable name cannot contain `-`, and
# `config` lowercases every key it reads. The name each definition has upstream travels as `NAME`.
#
# To load it into a shell — `export` takes the whole `NAME=value`, so descriptions containing
# spaces survive, which `source` would not manage:
#
#   while IFS= read -r line; do
#     [ -n "${line%%#*}" ] && export "$line"
#   done < config/cloudwatch_alarms.sandbox.env
#
# rds-deadlocks — Deadlocks on rds
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__NAME=rds-deadlocks
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__CLASSIFICATION=rds-alerts
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__METRIC_NAME=Deadlocks
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__NAMESPACE=AWS/RDS
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__DIMENSIONS=DBClusterIdentifier=hyperswitchdb-cluster
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__PERIOD=60
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__STATISTIC=Sum
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__SEVERITIES__SEV1__THRESHOLD=50
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__SEVERITIES__SEV1__COMPARISON_OPERATOR=GreaterThanThreshold
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__SEVERITIES__SEV1__EVALUATION_PERIODS=2
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__SEVERITIES__SEV1__TREAT_MISSING_DATA=notBreaching
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__SEVERITIES__SEV1__DESCRIPTION=SEV1: RDS cluster has critical deadlock rate. Immediate investigation required.
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__SEVERITIES__SEV2__THRESHOLD=20
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__SEVERITIES__SEV2__COMPARISON_OPERATOR=GreaterThanThreshold
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__SEVERITIES__SEV2__EVALUATION_PERIODS=2
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__SEVERITIES__SEV2__TREAT_MISSING_DATA=notBreaching
OBSERVABILITY__CLOUDWATCH__ALARMS__RDS_DEADLOCKS__SEVERITIES__SEV2__DESCRIPTION=SEV2: RDS cluster is experiencing high deadlock rate. Review transaction patterns.

